urrent), margin: PAT margin target >10% by FY28, order inflow: not applicable, capex/commissioning: ₹50Cr warehousing in Rajkot (Q2FY27), ₹20Cr dairy acquisition (closed), ₹15Cr cold storage (pending Coca-Cola agreement)","src":"concall","as_of":"Q4FY26"},"growth_optionality":{"title":"Growth verticals / optionality","body":"Roll-ups in Ayurvedic Cosmetics, Solar Tech, and AI/IT; international gateway via Dubai subsidiary (live in 15 days); potential warehousing partnerships or lease models to accelerate national expansion","src":"concall","as_of":"Q4FY26"},"margins":{"title":"Margins & cost dynamics","body":"Cost structure improving via vertical integration (dairy → milk → packaged products); warehousing CAPEX will yield 20-25% EBITDA margins post-commissioning due to strategic location and government subsidies; no margin pressure from raw material inflation cited","src":"concall","as_of":"Q4FY26"},"capital_allocation":{"title":"Capital allocation","body":"100% of raised capital allocated to acquisitions (dairy) and strategic CAPEX (warehousing, cold storage); no dividends planned; bonus issue possible; promoter equity to increase from 35% to 40% via warrants, targeting 51% by Q1FY28","src":"concall","as_of":"Q4FY26"},"management_tone":{"title":"Management quality / tone","body":"Confident, transparent, and investor-centric; management openly acknowledges lack of domain expertise in new verticals but emphasizes partner-driven execution; strong focus on EPS, asset creation, and mainboard migration; receptive to investor feedback on leasing models","src":"concall","as_of":"Q4FY26"},"risks":{"title":"Risks & watch-items","body":"Execution risk on multiple simultaneous acquisitions; delay in Coca-Cola agreement impacting cold storage commissioning; land acquisition delays in Maharashtra; regulatory scrutiny on promoter stake increase triggering open offer; overextension across unrelated verticals","src":"concall","as_of":"Q4FY26"},"non_obvious":{"title":"Non-obvious takeaways","body":"The ₹15Cr dairy acquisition for a ₹30Cr asset implies deep distress pricing — management is buying undervalued, asset-rich businesses with operational expertise but capital constraints; government subsidies (₹20Cr+) on warehousing effectively reduce net CAPEX by 40%, making ROI faster than market norms","src":"concall","as_of":"Q4FY26"},"challenges":{"title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers","body":"| Challenge | Beneficiary/Loser | Dir | Conviction | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Sonalis acquiring distressed dairy and warehousing assets at deep discounts | Sonalis Consumer Products Limited | beneficiary | High | Asset accretion and subsidy leverage create hidden value not reflected in current market cap |\n| Promoter equity increase via warrants to reach 51% by 2028 | Sonalis Consumer Products Limited | beneficiary | High | Reduces delisting risk, improves governance perception, and aligns incentives for mainboard migration |\n| Coca-Cola supply agreement pending for mango pulp cold storage | Sonalis Consumer Products Limited | loser | Medium | Delay in agreement directly postpones ₹15Cr cold storage commissioning and revenue ramp-up |","src":"concall","as_of":"Q4FY26"}}}